{"id":"mahabharata-12-286","work":"mahabharata","part":12,"partName":"शान्तिपर्व","partNameEn":"Shanti Parva","unit":286,"title":"षडशीत्यधिकद्विशततमोऽध्यायः","titleEn":"Adhyaya 286 · The body and the enemy of ignorance","summary":{"en":"Parashara says that no father, friend, teacher or wife is wholly without good, and describes the body as a mass of veins and bones. He says that ignorance is a man's one enemy, which drives him to terrible deeds, and so ends his teaching to the king of Videha.","kn":"ತಂದೆ, ಮಿತ್ರ, ಗುರು, ಪತ್ನಿ ಯಾರೂ ಸಂಪೂರ್ಣ ನಿರ್ಗುಣರಲ್ಲವೆಂದು ಪರಾಶರ ಹೇಳಿ ದೇಹವನ್ನು ನರ-ಮೂಳೆಗಳ ರಾಶಿಯೆಂದು ವರ್ಣಿಸುತ್ತಾನೆ. ಅಜ್ಞಾನವೇ ಮನುಷ್ಯನ ಏಕೈಕ ಶತ್ರು, ಅದು ಭಯಂಕರ ಕರ್ಮಗಳಿಗೆ ಪ್ರೇರಿಸುತ್ತದೆಂದು ಹೇಳಿ ವಿದೇಹ ರಾಜನಿಗೆ ಬೋಧನೆ ಮುಗಿಸುತ್ತಾನೆ.","hi":"पराशर कहते हैं कि पिता, मित्र, गुरु और स्त्री कोई भी पूर्णतः गुणहीन नहीं होता, और देह को नसों-हड्डियों का समूह बताते हैं। वे कहते हैं कि अज्ञान ही मनुष्य का एकमात्र शत्रु है जो उसे भयंकर कर्मों में लगाता है, और विदेहराज को उपदेश पूरा करते हैं।","te":"తండ్రి, స్నేహితుడు, గురువు, భార్య ఎవరూ పూర్తిగా గుణహీనులు కారని పరాశరుడు చెప్పి దేహాన్ని నరాలు, ఎముకల సమూహంగా వర్ణిస్తాడు. అజ్ఞానమే మనిషికి ఏకైక శత్రువని, అది భయంకర కర్మలకు ప్రేరేపిస్తుందని చెప్పి విదేహ రాజుకు బోధను ముగిస్తాడు.","ta":"தந்தை, நண்பன், குரு, மனைவி யாரும் முற்றிலும் குணமற்றவர் அல்லர் என்று பராசரர் கூறி, உடலை நரம்பும் எலும்பும் சேர்ந்த குவியலாக விவரிக்கிறார். அறியாமையே மனிதனின் ஒரே பகைவன், அது கொடிய செயல்களைச் செய்யத் தூண்டுகிறது என்று கூறி விதேக மன்னனுக்குப் போதனையை முடிக்கிறார்.","ml":"പിതാവോ സുഹൃത്തോ ഗുരുവോ ഭാര്യയോ ഒരിക്കലും പൂർണ്ണമായി നന്മയില്ലാത്തവരല്ലെന്ന് പരാശരൻ പറയുന്നു; ശരീരത്തെ ഞരമ്പുകളുടെയും അസ്ഥികളുടെയും കൂട്ടമായി അദ്ദേഹം വിവരിക്കുന്നു. മനുഷ്യന്റെ ഏക ശത്രു അജ്ഞതയാണെന്നും, അത് അവനെ ഭീകരമായ പ്രവൃത്തികളിലേക്ക് നയിക്കുന്നുവെന്നും പറഞ്ഞ് വിദേഹരാജാവിനുള്ള ഉപദേശം അദ്ദേഹം അവസാനിപ്പിക്കുന്നു."},"source":"Mahabharata, Critical Edition (BORI, Pune) 12.286; e-text by M. Tokunaga and J. D. Smith, © BORI 1999, version of Wed Jun 16 2021","sections":[{"title":"मोक्षधर्मपर्व","titleEn":"Mokshadharma Parva (Duties for liberation)","verses":[{"text":"पराशर उवाच","meaning":{"en":"Parashara said:"}},{"n":1,"text":"पिता सखायो गुरवः स्त्रियश्च\nन निर्गुणा नाम भवन्ति लोके ।\nअनन्यभक्ताः प्रियवादिनश्च\nहिताश्च वश्याश्च तथैव राजन् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Fathers, friends, teachers and wives are never without good qualities in this world, king, when they are single-hearted in devotion, pleasant in speech, well-wishing and obedient."}},{"n":2,"text":"पिता परं दैवतं मानवानां\nमातुर्विशिष्टं पितरं वदन्ति ।\nज्ञानस्य लाभं परमं वदन्ति\nजितेन्द्रियार्थाः परमाप्नुवन्ति ॥","meaning":{"en":"The father is the highest deity of men; they say the father surpasses the mother. They call the gaining of knowledge the highest gain, and those who have mastered the objects of the senses attain the highest."}},{"n":3,"text":"रणाजिरे यत्र शराग्निसंस्तरे\nनृपात्मजो घातमवाप्य दह्यते ।\nप्रयाति लोकानमरैः सुदुर्लभा-\nन्निषेवते स्वर्गफलं यथासुखम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"On the field of battle, on the bed of arrow-fire, a king's son who meets death and is burned there goes to worlds very hard for even the immortals to reach and enjoys the fruit of heaven at ease."}},{"n":4,"text":"श्रान्तं भीतं भ्रष्टशस्त्रं रुदन्तं\nपराङ्मुखं परिबर्हैश्च हीनम् ।\nअनुद्यतं रोगिणं याचमानं\nन वै हिंस्याद्बालवृद्धौ च राजन् ॥","meaning":{"en":"A king should not kill one who is weary, frightened, has lost his weapon, weeps, has turned away, is without supplies or has not taken up arms, who is sick or begging, or a child or an old man."}},{"n":5,"text":"परिबर्हैः सुसंपन्नमुद्यतं तुल्यतां गतम् ।\nअतिक्रमेत नृपतिः संग्रामे क्षत्रियात्मजम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"A Kshatriya's son in battle should be passed over by the king if he is well provided with supplies, is ready and is an equal."}},{"n":6,"text":"तुल्यादिह वधः श्रेयान्विशिष्टाच्चेति निश्चयः ।\nनिहीनात्कातराच्चैव नृपाणां गर्हितो वधः ॥","meaning":{"en":"It is settled that killing an equal or a superior is better in this world; for kings killing a very low or a cowardly man is censured."}},{"n":7,"text":"पापात्पापसमाचारान्निहीनाच्च नराधिप ।\nपाप एव वधः प्रोक्तो नरकायेति निश्चयः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Killing a sinner, one of sinful conduct, or a very low man, lord of men, is itself called a sin, leading to hell; so it is settled."}},{"n":8,"text":"न कश्चित्त्राति वै राजन्दिष्टान्तवशमागतम् ।\nसावशेषायुषं चापि कश्चिदेवापकर्षति ॥","meaning":{"en":"No one, king, saves a man who has come under the power of fate's end; yet someone may cut short even one who still has life remaining."}},{"n":9,"text":"स्निग्धैश्च क्रियमाणानि कर्माणीह निवर्तयेत् ।\nहिंसात्मकानि कर्माणि नायुरिच्छेत्परायुषा ॥","meaning":{"en":"One should hold back actions being done by loving friends that are violent; one should not wish for one's own life at the cost of another's."}},{"n":10,"text":"गृहस्थानां तु सर्वेषां विनाशमभिकाङ्क्षताम् ।\nनिधनं शोभनं तात पुलिनेषु क्रियावताम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"For all householders who desire destruction, an end on the river banks is fine for those who perform rites, dear one."}},{"n":11,"text":"आयुषि क्षयमापन्ने पञ्चत्वमुपगच्छति ।\nनाकारणात्तद्भवति कारणैरुपपादितम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"When life has reached its end, a man goes to death; it does not happen without cause but is brought about by causes."}},{"n":12,"text":"तथा शरीरं भवति देहाद्येनोपपादितम् ।\nअध्वानं गतकश्चायं प्राप्तश्चायं गृहाद्गृहम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"So the body arises, produced by that which comes from the body; and this one, having gone along the road, has come from house to house."}},{"n":13,"text":"द्वितीयं कारणं तत्र नान्यत्किंचन विद्यते ।\nतद्देहं देहिनां युक्तं मोक्षभूतेषु वर्तते ॥","meaning":{"en":"There is no second cause in that, nothing else at all; the body suited to embodied beings goes on among the elements that are the means of release."}},{"n":14,"text":"सिरास्नाय्वस्थिसंघातं बीभत्सामेध्यसंकुलम् ।\nभूतानामिन्द्रियाणां च गुणानां च समागमम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Learned thinkers on the self call the body, a mass of veins, sinews and bones filled with foul and impure matter, a union of the elements, the senses and the qualities, ending in skin."}},{"n":15,"text":"त्वगन्तं देहमित्याहुर्विद्वांसोऽध्यात्मचिन्तकाः ।\nगुणैरपि परिक्षीणं शरीरं मर्त्यतां गतम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"When the body is worn away by the qualities, it comes to mortality."}},{"n":16,"text":"शरीरिणा परित्यक्तं निश्चेष्टं गतचेतनम् ।\nभूतैः प्रकृतिमापन्नैस्ततो भूमौ निमज्जति ॥","meaning":{"en":"Abandoned by the embodied one, motionless and lifeless, it sinks to the ground as the elements return to their nature."}},{"n":17,"text":"भावितं कर्मयोगेन जायते तत्र तत्र ह ।\nइदं शरीरं वैदेह म्रियते यत्र तत्र ह ।\nतत्स्वभावोऽपरो दृष्टो विसर्गः कर्मणस्तथा ॥","meaning":{"en":"Shaped by the force of action, he is born here and there. This body, king of Videha, dies wherever it dies; another course is seen, determined by its nature and by action's release."}},{"n":18,"text":"न जायते तु नृपते कंचित्कालमयं पुनः ।\nपरिभ्रमति भूतात्मा द्यामिवाम्बुधरो महान् ॥","meaning":{"en":"But for a time, king, it is not born again; the soul among beings wanders as a great cloud wanders in the sky."}},{"n":19,"text":"स पुनर्जायते राजन्प्राप्येहायतनं नृप ।\nमनसः परमो ह्यात्मा इन्द्रियेभ्यः परं मनः ॥","meaning":{"en":"It is born again, king, on reaching a dwelling here. The self is beyond the mind, and the mind is beyond the senses."}},{"n":20,"text":"द्विविधानां च भूतानां जङ्गमाः परमा नृप ।\nजङ्गमानामपि तथा द्विपदाः परमा मताः ।\nद्विपदानामपि तथा द्विजा वै परमाः स्मृताः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Of the two kinds of creatures, the moving are highest, king; and among the moving, the two-footed are held highest; and among the two-footed, the twice-born are called the highest."}},{"n":21,"text":"द्विजानामपि राजेन्द्र प्रज्ञावन्तः परा मताः ।\nप्राज्ञानामात्मसंबुद्धाः संबुद्धानाममानिनः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Of the twice-born, king of kings, the wise are held highest; of the wise, those enlightened about the self; of the enlightened, those without pride."}},{"n":22,"text":"जातमन्वेति मरणं नृणामिति विनिश्चयः ।\nअन्तवन्ति हि कर्माणि सेवन्ते गुणतः प्रजाः ॥","meaning":{"en":"It is settled that death follows birth for men; and creatures follow actions that end, according to their qualities."}},{"n":23,"text":"आपन्ने तूत्तरां काष्ठां सूर्ये यो निधनं व्रजेत् ।\nनक्षत्रे च मुहूर्ते च पुण्ये राजन्स पुण्यकृत् ॥","meaning":{"en":"The man who meets death when the sun has reached its northern course, under an auspicious star and at an auspicious moment, king, is a doer of merit."}},{"n":24,"text":"अयोजयित्वा क्लेशेन जनं प्लाव्य च दुष्कृतम् ।\nमृत्युनाप्राकृतेनेह कर्म कृत्वात्मशक्तितः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Without causing people trouble and having washed away his bad deeds, with an unordinary death here he has done his work to the measure of his strength."}},{"n":25,"text":"विषमुद्बन्धनं दाहो दस्युहस्तात्तथा वधः ।\nदंष्ट्रिभ्यश्च पशुभ्यश्च प्राकृतो वध उच्यते ॥","meaning":{"en":"Poison, hanging, burning, killing at the hands of robbers, and by animals with fangs and other beasts is called an ordinary death."}},{"n":26,"text":"न चैभिः पुण्यकर्माणो युज्यन्ते नाभिसंधिजैः ।\nएवंविधैश्च बहुभिरपरैः प्राकृतैरपि ॥","meaning":{"en":"Those whose deeds are meritorious are not joined with these, nor with those born of intent, nor with many others of this ordinary kind."}},{"n":27,"text":"ऊर्ध्वं हित्वा प्रतिष्ठन्ते प्राणाः पुण्यकृतां नृप ।\nमध्यतो मध्यपुण्यानामधो दुष्कृतकर्मणाम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"The vital breaths of the meritorious depart upward, king; those of middling merit go out through the middle, and those of evil deeds go downward."}},{"n":28,"text":"एकः शत्रुर्न द्वितीयोऽस्ति शत्रु-\nरज्ञानतुल्यः पुरुषस्य राजन् ।\nयेनावृतः कुरुते संप्रयुक्तो\nघोराणि कर्माणि सुदारुणानि ॥","meaning":{"en":"There is one enemy, and no second enemy is equal to ignorance for a man, king; covered by it, he is set to work and does dreadful, very cruel deeds."}},{"n":29,"text":"प्रबोधनार्थं श्रुतिधर्मयुक्तं\nवृद्धानुपास्यं च भवेत यस्य ।\nप्रयत्नसाध्यो हि स राजपुत्र\nप्रज्ञाशरेणोन्मथितः परैति ॥","meaning":{"en":"For waking up, one should have the dharma taught by scripture and respect for the elders; a prince so equipped can, with effort, be brought to success; struck down by the arrow of wisdom, the enemy goes away."}},{"n":30,"text":"अधीत्य वेदांस्तपसा ब्रह्मचारी\nयज्ञाञ्शक्त्या संनिसृज्येह पञ्च ।\nवनं गच्छेत्पुरुषो धर्मकामः\nश्रेयश्चित्वा स्थापयित्वा स्ववंशम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Having studied the Vedas as a celibate student with austerity, having performed the five sacrifices as he can, a man seeking dharma should go to the forest, having gathered merit and established his own line."}},{"n":31,"text":"उपभोगैरपि त्यक्तं नात्मानमवसादयेत् ।\nचण्डालत्वेऽपि मानुष्यं सर्वथा तात दुर्लभम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"One should not depress oneself even when abandoned by pleasures; even in the state of a Chandala, human birth is in every way hard to get, dear one."}},{"n":32,"text":"इयं हि योनिः प्रथमा यां प्राप्य जगतीपते ।\nआत्मा वै शक्यते त्रातुं कर्मभिः शुभलक्षणैः ॥","meaning":{"en":"For this is the first birth, king, and having reached it one can save oneself by actions with good marks."}},{"n":33,"text":"कथं न विप्रणश्येम योनितोऽस्या इति प्रभो ।\nकुर्वन्ति धर्मं मनुजाः श्रुतिप्रामाण्यदर्शनात् ॥","meaning":{"en":"\"How may we not be lost from this birth?\" thinking so, lord, people practice dharma, seeing the authority of scripture."}},{"n":34,"text":"यो दुर्लभतरं प्राप्य मानुष्यमिह वै नरः ।\nधर्मावमन्ता कामात्मा भवेत्स खलु वञ्च्यते ॥","meaning":{"en":"A man who has obtained the very rare human birth here and then scorns dharma and is given over to desire is certainly cheated."}},{"n":35,"text":"यस्तु प्रीतिपुरोगेण चक्षुषा तात पश्यति ।\nदीपोपमानि भूतानि यावदर्चिर्न नश्यति ॥","meaning":{"en":"He who looks with a loving eye, dear one, on beings as like lamps, as long as the flame has not died,"}},{"n":36,"text":"सान्त्वेनानुप्रदानेन प्रियवादेन चाप्युत ।\nसमदुःखसुखो भूत्वा स परत्र महीयते ॥","meaning":{"en":"having become the same in sorrow and joy, by comfort, by giving and by kind speech, is honored in the next world."}},{"n":37,"text":"दानं त्यागः शोभना मूर्तिरद्भ्यो\nभूयः प्लाव्यं तपसा वै शरीरम् ।\nसरस्वतीनैमिषपुष्करेषु\nये चाप्यन्ये पुण्यदेशाः पृथिव्याम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Giving, renunciation, a fair appearance, and bathing the body in waters again and again with austerity, at the Sarasvati, Naimisha, Pushkara and other holy places of the earth,"}},{"n":38,"text":"गृहेषु येषामसवः पतन्ति\nतेषामथो निर्हरणं प्रशस्तम् ।\nयानेन वै प्रापणं च श्मशाने\nशौचेन नूनं विधिना चैव दाहः ॥","meaning":{"en":"for those in whose houses the breath departs, taking out the body is praised, with conveyance to the cremation ground by a vehicle, and cremation with purity and by rule."}},{"n":39,"text":"इष्टिः पुष्टिर्यजनं याजनं च\nदानं पुण्यानां कर्मणां च प्रयोगः ।\nशक्त्या पित्र्यं यच्च किंचित्प्रशस्तं\nसर्वाण्यात्मार्थे मानवो यः करोति ॥","meaning":{"en":"Sacrificial offerings, nourishment, performing and having others perform sacrifice, giving, and the practice of meritorious deeds, and whatever is praised in ancestral rites done as one can: the man who does all of this does it for his own good."}},{"n":40,"text":"धर्मशास्त्राणि वेदाश्च षडङ्गानि नराधिप ।\nश्रेयसोऽर्थे विधीयन्ते नरस्याक्लिष्टकर्मणः ॥","meaning":{"en":"The treatises on dharma, the Vedas and the six limbs, lord of men, are laid down for the highest good of a man whose actions are untroubled."}},{"text":"भीष्म उवाच","meaning":{"en":"Bhishma said:"}},{"n":41,"text":"एतद्वै सर्वमाख्यातं मुनिना सुमहात्मना ।\nविदेहराजाय पुरा श्रेयसोऽर्थे नराधिप ॥","meaning":{"en":"All this was told long ago by that great-souled sage to the king of Videha, lord of men, for the sake of the highest good."}}]}]}